{
  "query": "AeroCity Utilities operates about 40,000 smart meters that send electricity usage readings every second into Google Cloud. The company plans to perform near real time usage analysis, demand prediction, and capacity planning based on these telemetry streams. The platform team wants a fully managed solution that can scale massively, align with a multi cloud strategy, and provide low latency for both ingestion and query workloads. Which solution should they implement?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Use Pub/Sub with Dataflow and BigQuery and Looker Studio",
      "explanation": "This approach ingests streams with Pub/Sub, processes them with Dataflow, stores data in BigQuery, and visualizes it in Looker Studio",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Spanner and Looker Studio",
      "explanation": "Cloud Spanner is a globally distributed relational service that integrates with business intelligence tools such as Looker Studio",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Provision a multi cloud MongoDB Atlas cluster and use Charts",
      "explanation": "MongoDB Atlas is a fully managed database that can span multiple clouds and includes native visualization with Charts",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Bigtable and Looker",
      "explanation": "Bigtable is a managed wide column store that offers very high throughput and integrates with Looker for reporting",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    }
  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct choice is <b>Provision a multi cloud MongoDB Atlas cluster and use Charts</b>. It meets the need for a fully managed service that spans multiple cloud providers and it delivers low latency at scale for both ingestion and query workloads.</p><p>Atlas offers multi cloud clusters across Google Cloud, AWS, and Azure which aligns directly with a multi cloud strategy. Its time series collections and horizontal scaling handle very high write rates from telemetry streams while still enabling efficient time range and aggregation queries. Charts provides built in real time visualization on top of the same dataset, so you can analyze usage and demand with minimal pipeline complexity and consistently low latency.</p><p><i>Use Pub/Sub with Dataflow and BigQuery and Looker Studio</i> is fully managed and scales well, but it anchors analytics to a single cloud and streaming data can have short but nonzero query availability delays in BigQuery which makes consistently low latency interactive queries more challenging for per second telemetry.</p><p><i>Use Cloud Spanner and Looker Studio</i> provides strong transactional consistency and global scale for relational workloads, yet it is not optimized for high volume time series analytics and it does not satisfy a multi cloud requirement.</p><p><i>Use Bigtable and Looker</i> is excellent for low latency time series storage on Google Cloud, but it lacks native SQL style analytics and the named BI tool does not directly query Bigtable, which adds more components and remains single cloud.</p>",
